            <p>Hepatic Biloma on Computed Tomography. This image shows a well-defined, low-attenuation fluid collection adjacent to the liver, consistent with a hepatic biloma. The lesion appears hypodense compared to the surrounding hepatic parenchyma, with smooth margins and no internal enhancement, typical of a contained bile leak accumulating in the subcapsular region. Contributed by R Kabir, MD</p>
